就这些了。

1468
00:57:04.540 --> 00:57:04.900
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1469
00:57:05.800 --> 00:57:07.020
Because guess what?
因为你猜怎么着？

1470
00:57:07.180 --> 00:57:09.080
Nicole finally returns to her desk.
妮可终于回到了她的办公桌前。

1471
00:57:09.220 --> 00:57:12.160
She sees the letter from the editor written by Esmeralda.
她看到了埃斯梅拉达写的给编辑的信。

1472
00:57:12.160 --> 00:57:18.920
Yeah, and it's just basically a letter from Ned's point of view saying that he stole this
没错，那基本上就是一封以内德的口吻写的信，说他从一个名叫埃斯梅拉达的女人那里

1473
00:57:18.920 --> 00:57:25.460
job from a woman named Esmeralda who has a banging body despite being a single mother.
偷走了这份工作，而那个女人尽管是单身母亲，却有着火辣的身材。

1474
00:57:25.600 --> 00:57:27.960
It's just all about Esmeralda and her awesome body.
信里全是关于埃斯梅拉达和她那迷人的身材的内容。

1475
00:57:28.100 --> 00:57:29.900
Yeah, and how he took her job.
没错，还有他是如何抢走她的工作的。

1476
00:57:30.100 --> 00:57:32.540
So clearly, they can't use that.
所以很显然，他们不能用那封信。

1477
00:57:32.700 --> 00:57:32.980
No.
不能。

1478
00:57:33.100 --> 00:57:34.580
So Nicole just deletes it.
于是妮可直接把它删了。

1479
00:57:35.040 --> 00:57:39.960
Mare is going to have a talking head where she says it's 538 and she doesn't know what
梅尔会有一个访谈镜头，她说现在是5点38分，她不知道

1480
00:57:39.960 --> 00:57:40.820
they're going to print.
他们要刊登什么。

1481
00:57:40.820 --> 00:57:44.260
Maybe she'll just type up the train schedules to be safe.
也许为了保险起见，她会直接把火车时刻表打出来。

1482
00:57:44.580 --> 00:57:46.780
And lady, this made me curious.
而且，女士，这让我很好奇。

1483
00:57:47.060 --> 00:57:47.480
What?
什么？

1484
00:57:47.800 --> 00:57:49.840
I was curious about the 6 p.m.
我对他们面临的下午6点的

1485
00:57:49.940 --> 00:57:51.280
deadline that they're up againSt.
截止日期感到好奇。

1486
00:57:51.500 --> 00:57:55.520
And then I started researching what the hours are like to get a newspaper out into the world.
于是我开始研究出版一份报纸需要什么样的工时。

1487
00:57:55.520 --> 00:58:00.920
And I found this fantastic YouTube video about a local newspaper in Singapore called The Straits
我找到了一个关于新加坡一家名为《海峡时报》的当地报纸的精彩YouTube视频。

1488
00:58:00.920 --> 00:58:01.360
Times.
《海峡时报》。

1489
00:58:01.660 --> 00:58:05.400
And they sort of take you through their night getting a newspaper out.
他们带你了解了他们通宵出报的过程。

1490
00:58:05.560 --> 00:58:07.200
It starts at 5.30 p.m.
从下午5点30分开始。

1491
00:58:07.200 --> 00:58:11.860
And all throughout the night, different articles and headlines are coming together and they're
整个晚上，不同的文章和标题汇集在一起，然后他们

1492
00:58:11.860 --> 00:58:12.160
printing.
进行印刷。

1493
00:58:12.420 --> 00:58:14.860
And their day ends at 5.30 a.m.
他们的一天在凌晨5点30分结束。

1494
00:58:15.020 --> 00:58:20.120
So whoever Ned is turning this over to is going to be the night shift that is then going to
所以无论内德把工作交给谁，那都将是夜班人员，他们会在天亮前

1495
00:58:20.120 --> 00:58:23.040
get this newspaper out by daybreak.
把报纸发出去。

1496
00:58:23.240 --> 00:58:23.540
Wow.
哇。

1497
00:58:23.840 --> 00:58:25.400
It's a really interesting existence.
这真是一种有趣的生活方式。

1498
00:58:25.660 --> 00:58:28.680
Like the man that was showing you around the newspaper in Singapore said, you know,
就像那个带你参观新加坡报社的人说的，你知道，

1499
00:58:28.820 --> 00:58:31.560
his wife is leaving for work when he's getting home.
当他到家时，他的妻子正要去上班。

1500
00:58:31.840 --> 00:58:32.060
Yeah.
是啊。

1501
00:58:32.060 --> 00:58:32.440
Yeah.
没错。

1502
00:58:32.760 --> 00:58:35.140
So shout out to the night shift at the newspaper.
所以要向报社的夜班员工致敬。

1503
00:58:35.460 --> 00:58:35.920
Yes.
是的。

1504
00:58:36.140 --> 00:58:36.580
Thank you.
谢谢。

1505
00:58:36.960 --> 00:58:38.080
Well, guess what?
好吧，你猜怎么着？

1506
00:58:38.280 --> 00:58:44.000
Their final article, the one thing they thought they still had, this Crime Beat article, is
他们的最后一篇报道，也就是他们以为自己还拥有的那篇“犯罪专栏”文章，

1507
00:58:44.000 --> 00:58:45.560
also going to fall apart.
也要泡汤了。

1508
00:58:45.740 --> 00:58:46.180
Yeah.
是啊。

1509
00:58:46.380 --> 00:58:53.040
Because what they realized is that the morgue called the police to say that some creep called
因为他们意识到，停尸房给警察打了电话，说有个怪人打电话给他们，

1510
00:58:53.040 --> 00:58:57.780
them, insisting that there was a body they didn't know about and they needed to look around
坚称有一具他们不知道的尸体，要求他们四处找找。

1511
00:58:57.780 --> 00:58:58.320
for it.
找找看。

1512
00:58:58.400 --> 00:59:00.140
And we realized it was Ned.
我们意识到那个人是内德。

1513
00:59:00.140 --> 00:59:04.060
Yeah, Ned's really quickly, like, hangs up because he's like, oh, crap.
没错，内德很快就挂断了电话，因为他心想，糟了。

1514
00:59:04.200 --> 00:59:05.080
Ned's like, oh, no.
内德心想，噢，不。

1515
00:59:05.280 --> 00:59:06.980
So there's no serial killer.
所以根本没有连环杀手。

1516
00:59:07.240 --> 00:59:08.220
There's no nothing.
什么都没有。

1517
00:59:08.660 --> 00:59:12.900
So Ned has to quickly bang out a letter from the editor.
所以内德不得不赶紧写出一封编辑信。

1518
00:59:13.140 --> 00:59:16.680
And he decides to title it, No News is Good News.
他决定将其命名为“没有新闻就是好新闻”。

1519
00:59:16.920 --> 00:59:17.340
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1520
00:59:17.780 --> 00:59:21.940
And he says that's not something you expect to hear from the editor-in-chief of the town
他说，这可不是你会从镇报主编口中听到的那种话。

1521
00:59:21.940 --> 00:59:22.480
newspaper.
但犯罪率的降低，证明了人们珍视自己的社区。

1522
00:59:23.000 --> 00:59:26.680
But a lack of crime is evidence of people who treasure their community.
于是他发表了这封很长的信，为了凑字数，他最后竟然抄袭了埃尔莫·伦纳德的小说。

1523
00:59:27.900 --> 00:59:34.880
And so he releases this very long letter, which in order to pad it, he just ends up kind
比如《52张牌》。

1524
00:59:34.880 --> 00:59:38.500
of plagiarizing Elmore Leonard's novels.
听起来他直接把其中的几章内容放进去了。

1525
00:59:38.780 --> 00:59:39.720
52 Pickup.
是的。

1526
00:59:39.860 --> 00:59:43.260
He just includes a few chapters of it, it sounds like.
还有《矮子当道》。

1527
00:59:43.300 --> 00:59:43.560
Yes.
没错。

1528
00:59:43.700 --> 00:59:44.540
And Get Shorty.
有一个很棒的转场镜头。

1529
00:59:44.740 --> 00:59:45.020
Yeah.
是奥斯卡。

1530
00:59:45.240 --> 00:59:46.940
There is a great cutaway.
他在外面。

1531
00:59:47.180 --> 00:59:47.780
It's Oscar.
他在报刊亭。

1532
00:59:47.940 --> 00:59:48.520
He's outside.
他在拿报纸。

1533
00:59:48.520 --> 00:59:49.900
He's at the newspaper stand.
他非常兴奋地想看数独谜题，因为那是他出的。

1534
00:59:49.900 --> 00:59:51.100
He's picking up the paper.
是的。

1535
00:59:51.100 --> 00:59:56.080
And he's really excited to see the Sudoku puzzle because he created it.
我们之前不知道是谁出的，但现在揭晓了，是奥斯卡。

1536
00:59:56.220 --> 00:59:56.440
Yes.
奥斯卡给斯坦利打电话说，斯坦利，你觉得怎么样？

1537
00:59:56.540 --> 00:59:59.720
We didn't know who did it, but it's revealed it was Oscar.
没错。

1538
01:00:00.060 --> 01:00:03.760
And Oscar calls Stanley and is like, Stanley, what'd you think?
他给斯坦利发了一张照片。

1539
01:00:04.140 --> 01:00:04.480
Yeah.
他说，噢，你肯定会说这太简单了，斯坦利，当然了。

1540
01:00:04.540 --> 01:00:05.960
He sends him a picture of it.
这是一段非常可爱的对话。

1541
01:00:06.160 --> 01:00:10.480
And he's like, oh, you would say it's too easy, Stanley, of course.
这表明奥斯卡仍然和斯坦利有联系。

1542
01:00:10.620 --> 01:00:12.040
It's a very cute exchange.
是啊。

1543
01:00:12.040 --> 01:00:14.660
And it shows that Oscar's still in touch with Stanley.
这可能暗示了奥斯卡仍然与邓德·米夫林公司的其他人保持着联系。

1544
01:00:14.960 --> 01:00:15.240
Yeah.
是的。

1545
01:00:15.240 --> 01:00:20.660
And it may be hints to the fact that Oscar is still in touch with other people from Dunder
好吧，这一集将以梅尔的采访镜头结束。

1546
01:00:20.660 --> 01:00:21.100
Mifflin.
她说，你知道，虽然不完美，但这毕竟是他出的第一期报纸。

1547
01:00:21.300 --> 01:00:21.620
Yes.
她把它装裱起来，挂在了走廊里，就在其他古董旁边。

1548
01:00:21.880 --> 01:00:24.560
Well, the episode is going to end with a mare talking head.
没错。

1549
01:00:24.960 --> 01:00:27.840
She says, you know, it wasn't perfect, but it was his first issue.
是啊。

1550
01:00:28.380 --> 01:00:32.520
And she framed it and she put it in the hallway next to the other antiques.
是的。

1551
01:00:32.680 --> 01:00:33.680
It's very, very sweet.
这真的非常、非常贴心。

1552
01:00:33.960 --> 01:00:34.160
Yeah.
是啊。

1553
01:00:34.500 --> 01:00:37.560
Well, you know, this episode was directed by Ken Quapis.
嗯，你们知道，这一集是由肯·夸皮斯执导的。

1554
01:00:37.740 --> 01:00:43.260
And we did reach out to him because I wanted to know, what was it like to return to the world
我们确实联系了他，因为我想知道，重回伪纪录片的世界是什么感觉，

1555
01:00:43.260 --> 01:00:45.440
of mockumentary and did you have any challenges?
以及你是否遇到了什么挑战？

1556
01:00:45.900 --> 01:00:47.720
He wrote us back such a lovely email.
他回了一封非常可爱的邮件给我们。

1557
01:00:47.900 --> 01:00:48.500
He did.
确实如此。

1558
01:00:48.860 --> 01:00:51.720
I remembered something that Greg told us when we visited.
我记得格雷格去探班时告诉过我们一些事。

1559
01:00:51.980 --> 01:00:57.240
He said, when we designed this space, we wanted it to look very different from Dunder Mifflin.
他说，当我们设计这个空间时，我们希望它看起来和邓德·米夫林公司截然不同。

1560
01:00:57.380 --> 01:01:02.660
And they also researched what these old newspaper buildings looked like.
而且他们还研究了那些老报社大楼的样子。

1561
01:01:02.800 --> 01:01:04.360
And they were big and expansive.
它们又大又宽敞。

1562
01:01:04.680 --> 01:01:08.240
And beautiful old grand buildings with the big windows.
还有那些带有大窗户的漂亮古老建筑。

1563
01:01:08.680 --> 01:01:09.180
Yes.
没错。

1564
01:01:13.260 --> 01:01:15.920
So different from the Dunder Mifflin bullpen.
和邓德·米夫林的办公区完全不同。

1565
01:01:16.080 --> 01:01:19.940
He said it was a challenge to visually connect people in the space.
他说要在视觉上把空间里的人联系起来是一个挑战。

1566
01:01:20.600 --> 01:01:25.580
He said he was very grateful that this opened with a conference room scene because he could
他说他非常庆幸这一集是以会议室场景开场的，因为他可以

1567
01:01:25.580 --> 01:01:30.340
get everybody in the same room and really tell the story of who people were and connect them.
把所有人都聚在同一个房间里，真正讲述每个人的故事并将他们联系起来。

1568
01:01:30.500 --> 01:01:33.800
And he certainly has a lot of experience with conference room scenes.
而且他在会议室场景方面确实经验丰富。

1569
01:01:33.800 --> 01:01:40.400
But he also confirmed what Greg said, which was spy shots were difficult because when they
但他同时也证实了格雷格所说的话，那就是偷拍镜头很难拍，因为当他们

1570
01:01:40.400 --> 01:01:43.640
were designing the set, the set was designed by Susie Mancini, by the way.
设计布景时——顺便说一下，布景是由苏西·曼奇尼设计的——

1571
01:01:44.000 --> 01:01:47.240
And Greg said, I want you to use different blinds.
格雷格说，我希望你们用不同的百叶窗。

1572
01:01:47.260 --> 01:01:47.440
Yeah.
是啊。

1573
01:01:47.660 --> 01:01:49.260
Because I don't want it to look like Dunder Mifflin.
因为我不希望它看起来像邓德·米夫林。

1574
01:01:49.400 --> 01:01:51.960
So they chose these like tinier blinds.
所以他们选了这种比较小的百叶窗。

1575
01:01:52.160 --> 01:01:56.000
But then when you open them, it's really hard to do spy shots through them.
但当你打开它们时，透过它们拍偷拍镜头真的很难。

1576
01:01:56.280 --> 01:01:56.460
Yeah.
没错。

1577
01:01:56.700 --> 01:01:59.840
The blinds being a bigger size was a good thing.
百叶窗尺寸大一点其实是件好事。

1578
01:01:59.840 --> 01:02:00.440
Yes.
是的。

1579
01:02:00.720 --> 01:02:04.600
But overall, Ken was just so happy to be back working with these people.
但总的来说，肯非常高兴能回来和这些人一起工作。

1580
01:02:04.780 --> 01:02:07.140
He said it's an amazing group of actors.
他说这是一群了不起的演员。

1581
01:02:07.420 --> 01:02:08.580
And he had a great time.
他度过了一段美好的时光。

1582
01:02:08.800 --> 01:02:11.420
Well, I love that Ken is part of this world, too.
嗯，我很高兴肯也是这个世界的一部分。

1583
01:02:11.560 --> 01:02:14.280
And I love seeing all the little crossover moments.
我也很喜欢看到所有这些小小的联动时刻。

1584
01:02:14.580 --> 01:02:16.780
But I'm excited to get to know these characters.
但我很期待去了解这些角色。

1585
01:02:17.180 --> 01:02:18.240
Yeah, I agree.
是的，我同意。

1586
01:02:18.560 --> 01:02:19.600
Well, listen, everybody.
好了，各位，听着。

1587
01:02:19.800 --> 01:02:21.980
That's your breakdown of The Paper, Episode 2.
以上就是《报社》第二集的解析。

1588
01:02:21.980 --> 01:02:26.280
A big thank you to Kelly Cantley, Ken Kwapis, Chelsea Frye.
非常感谢凯莉·坎特利、肯·夸皮斯、切尔西·弗莱。

1589
01:02:26.340 --> 01:02:28.280
And Scott McGinnis, the Prop Master.
还有道具师斯科特·麦金尼斯。

1590
01:02:28.280 --> 01:02:31.240
Thanks for answering our questions when we reached out.
感谢你们在我们联系时回答了我们的问题。

1591
01:02:31.420 --> 01:02:33.200
And we'll see you guys all next week.
我们下周再见。

1592
01:02:33.380 --> 01:02:33.940
See you then.
到时见。

1593
01:02:34.340 --> 01:02:38.960
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

